from claude review, filtered down to the actually useful stuff (lots of duplication with above though):
- Request Body Not Proxied (proxy.rs:145, 156)
  Fix: Implement proper body reading and forwarding
- Unvalidated app_installation_id (provider.rs:28)
  Installation ID directly interpolated into URL without numeric validation Risk: Potential URL injection
- No GitHub Permissions Validation (permissions.rs)
  Invalid permissions silently accepted, fail only at runtime
- No CEL Rule Validation at Parse Time (rule.rs:29-31)
  Invalid CEL expressions only fail when requests arrive
  Fix: Validate with sample claims during rule loading
- HTTP Method Validation Missing (rule.rs:94)
  Fix: Whitelist standard HTTP methods only
- Response Headers Not Proxied (proxy.rs:163)
  Missing rate limits, ETag, pagination links, Content-Type, etc.
  Impact: Clients can't handle pagination or rate limiting
- Request Headers Not Filtered (proxy.rs:148)
  No whitelist/validation of forwarded headers
- No Request Timeouts
  HTTP requests can hang indefinitely
  Fix: Add configurable timeouts
- Connection Pooling Not Reused (proxy.rs:147)
  New reqwest::Client created per request
  Impact: Connection overhead, no reuse
- No Configuration Validation (server.rs)
  Doesn't check if ruleset_dir exists, URLs valid, etc.
  Fix: Validate all config at startup
- No TLS Documentation
  Server binds to plain TCP; TLS must be external
  Fix: Document requirement for reverse proxy/TLS termination
- GCP KMS Creates New Client Per Request (lib.rs:113, 134)
  Resource overhead and potential connection exhaustion
- Inconsistent Safety Policy Enforcement
  #![deny(clippy::unwrap_used)] not applied to all crates
  Some crates use .expect() liberally despite policy
- Missing Claims Parsing Tests (claims.rs:142)
  No tests for critical claim extraction logic
- Incomplete Documentation (README.md:47-55)
